// SesiDo Coder Tool
allow "../../build/index" in as SesiDo; set_alias("SesiDo-Pro", "gemini-3.1-pro-preview"); set_alias("SesiDo-Flash", "gemini-3-flash-preview"); let logTag = "[" + SesiDo.universalTime + "]"; show logTag + " [CODER]"; SesiDo.writeCode(args); show "[CODER FINISHED]"

/*

    To use:

        npm run gen:code "a photo of a cat"

    SesiDo will spawn a child Sesi interpreter, set the appropriate aliases, show logging tags, and then invoke this script.

    Args:

        args: An object with the following key:

            prompt: (string, required) The user's natural-language request for code.

    Output:

        This script will write the artifact to SesiDo/.artifacts/code and return the artifact path if successful.

    Supported Models & Quality:

        - Primary Model: gemini-3.1-pro-preview (alias: SesiDo-Pro)
        - Secondary Model: gemini-3-flash-preview (alias: SesiDo-Flash)
        - Optimized For: Python, HTML/CSS/JS, Bash, JSON, Sesi configuration
        - Quality: Production-ready, well-commented, lint-safe code

    Artifact Location:

        The script will save the generated code to:

            ./SesiDo/.artifacts/code/{prompt}-{timestamp}.md

        where {timestamp} is the UTC ISO8601 timestamp when the code was
        generated. The artifact_path will include this full path.

    Safety & Environment:

        - This script runs in an isolated Sesi sandbox.
        - It does not have write access to system directories.
        - All file operations are restricted to the ./SesiDo/.artifacts/code/
          directory.
        - The environment is read-only except for artifact creation.

    Dependencies:

        allow "../../build/index" in with SesiDo;

        The agent must not attempt to write to arbitrary paths. This script
        strictly controls output to ./SesiDo/.artifacts/code/ to prevent system
        contamination.
*/